  "title": "Bonn intracranial EEG segments, sets C, D and E (Andrzejak et al. 2001)",
  "description": "This dataset contains 300 single-channel intracranial EEG segments (23.6 s each, 173.61 Hz) from five epilepsy patients, corresponding to sets C, D and E of the Bonn EEG dataset of Andrzejak et al. (2001). Sets C and D are seizure-free interictal recordings from hippocampal formations (opposite hemisphere and epileptogenic zone, respectively), and set E contains ictal activity. The data are a lossless BIDS re-packaging of the published text files, pooled under a single pseudo-subject because segment-to-patient mapping is unavailable.",
  "methods_description": "Segments were cut from continuous presurgical multichannel EEG recordings from depth and strip electrodes, selected after visual artifact inspection and a weak-stationarity criterion. Signals were recorded with a 128-channel amplifier using an average common reference, 12-bit digitization at 173.61 Hz, and band-pass filtering at 0.53-40 Hz. Source text files were converted to BrainVision format without filtering, resampling, re-referencing or rescaling.",
